
Step 1: Open Google Colab

Create a new Google Colab notebook or open the notebook provided in `/Final Code`.

Step 2: Copy and Paste Code Blocks

The code is organized into three sections intended to run one at a time in Google Colab. Copy and paste each code block into separate cells in Colab.

Step 3: Upload Required Files to your computer

Upload the following files into the Colab environment:

* best.pt trained model weights
* Traffic video files under "Original Video Used for Final Video"

Step 5: Run the Code Sections

Part 5a: Model Training (Optional)
This section was used to fine-tune the YOLO model using the VisDrone dataset. Since the trained model (`best.pt`) is provided, you have the option to run it. 
If you want to run more than 3 epochs, please change the number of epoch and run cell 1 again. 

Part 5b: Detection and Tracking
This setup cell installs the required tracking dependencies and configures the SORT tracker.
Running this cell helps avoid file conflictions and download a clean copy of SORT repository. 

Part 5C: Classifcation, MPH, Merging and CSV Files
* Run this cell
* Load the trained model (`best.pt`) in "YOLO Trained Model Called Best"
* Load the traffic analysis video in the file "Original Video Used for Final Video".
* Wait until all files and videos are downlaoded. 

